    <ImplementationPlan>
      <T-001>
        <Title>kafedra-flow-intake: define lifecycle, filter and reversible row-decision states</Title>
        <DependsOn></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The common path reaches current or archived plans in one action and exposes secondary filters without losing search or period context.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Source-row decisions distinguish immediate, confirmable and blocked impact and always preserve a restoration path.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Error, repeated request, no-result, offline and partial-success states retain the current plan, filter values and row editor.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run docs:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-001>
      <T-002>
        <Title>kafedra-design: adapt proven segmented, toolbar and bounded disclosure patterns</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-001 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The visible hierarchy is lifecycle, search, period, filters and one primary plan action; controls use existing Kafedra tokens and surfaces.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>The design records adaptations from Docomator segmented controls and Planer Solving sticky operator controls without copying assets or introducing a new framework.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Desktop, mobile, keyboard, 320 pixel width, long Russian labels and focus restoration are specified before implementation.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-002>
      <T-003>
        <Title>kafedra-motion: use no-motion for commits and restrained disclosure continuity</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-002 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Lifecycle and source-row decision commits use no-motion and update semantic state immediately.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>The filters disclosure uses only a short interruptible opacity and small translation transition; reduced motion is instant.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>No movement changes hit-target geometry or delays an operational action.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-003>
      <T-004>
        <Title>kafedra-data: add reversible inclusion authority and recovery-safe migration</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-003 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>Migration 032 is additive, records current decision plus append-only history and preserves all source and evidence fields.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Exclusion snapshots only the projection states changed by the decision; restoration does not overwrite later edits.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>Clean install, exact-base upgrade, repeated migration, integrity checks, verified backup, restore and forced-failure rollback pass.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>node --test tests/plan-source-rows-migration.test.mjs tests/plan-source-row-decisions.test.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-004>
      <T-005>
        <Title>kafedra-feature: implement API, domain projections and responsive plans UI</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-004 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The API enforces plan edit ACL, returns impact before a confirmable decision and rejects materialization of excluded rows.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>The toolbar and disclosure replace the lifecycle select and overloaded grid without duplicate controls.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>No-impact exclude, impact confirmation, blocked completed work, undo and restore all operate on persisted truth.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>node --test tests/plan-source-rows.test.mjs tests/plan-source-row-decisions.test.mjs tests/lifecycle.test.mjs</Command></Verification>
      </T-005>
      <T-006>
        <Title>kafedra-design-audit: independently inspect hierarchy, overflow, focus and decision clarity</Title>
        <DependsOn><T-005 /></DependsOn>
        <AcceptanceCriteria>
          <Criterion>The audit returns PASS, REVISE or BLOCK with actual desktop, mobile, keyboard and reduced-motion evidence.</Criterion>
          <Criterion>No blocker or major issue remains in one-click lifecycle, filter bounds, source visibility, impact wording or restoration discoverability.</Criterion>
        </AcceptanceCriteria>
        <Verification><Command>npm run design:check</Command></Verification>
      </T-006>
